 ],
 "balloons": [
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "HERALD"
   ],
   "text": "Listen and witness.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "HERALD"
   ],
   "text": "His Highness Sree Anizham Thirunal Marthanda Varma, Maharaja of Travancore.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-04",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "HERALD"
   ],
   "text": "Victor of Colachel. Breaker of the Eight Houses.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "From this day, I am no longer king of this land.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I am only the servant of He who lies here.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "All that I have taken, all that I have built, all that I have paid for in blood and exile and broken houses...",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I give to Him. The kingdom is His. I merely hold it in trust.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF (whisper)"
   ],
   "text": "He has given the land to god, so that he can keep it forever.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF (whisper)"
   ],
   "text": "Who can take from a god what a god owns? Not Mysore. Not the Nizam. Not the Dutch.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF (whisper)"
   ],
   "text": "Not even a woman with a legitimate claim.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "PRIESTS"
   ],
   "text": "Padmanabha Dasa.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "temple_priest",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "She reached Kochi. They gave her a small house. She tends a garden now.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I am glad she lives.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Are you?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "You could have let her go. During the battle. You were close enough.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "She was trying to reach the boats.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I did not see her.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Liar.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-04",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Perhaps.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "You have made your choice. Completely now. There is no more standing with one foot in each river.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "You are his man. His sword. His builder.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-05",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Yes.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "And I am still hers. Her kinswoman. Her blood. The one who stood beside you in the same hall while you burned her claim.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Velinadu sent no men against us. You kept your doors closed.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Closed is not the same as open.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Silence is not the same as support.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "We will not be enemies. Velinadu and Travancore need each other too much for that.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "But we will never be simple. You chose. So did I.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "What did you choose?",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "To remember.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "When everyone else forgets what this cost, I will remember. Savitri's face. Her garden in Kochi. The laugh she will never laugh again.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Someone has to carry that weight. It will not be you. It will not be him.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "So it will be me.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "The Nizam sent an envoy last month. Mysore's man was here before that.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "The British build at Madras as if they mean to stay forever. And the Dutch, even now, count their losses and plan their next move.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "This is what I was always building toward. Not conquering for glory. Consolidating for survival.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Every house I absorbed, every chief I bent, every woman I exiled, it was all for this:",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "a kingdom strong enough that when they come, any of them, all of them, they will find more than pepper and prayers.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And the cost?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "The cost is that men like Savitri's kinsman die in rooms they cannot leave.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "That women like her tend gardens in foreign cities and curse my name.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "That Revathi looks at me like I am the disease I claimed to cure.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Do you think I do not feel it? Do you think I do not wake in the night and hear them?",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Every name. Every claim I denied. Every law I bent or broke.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I remember her laugh. From when we were young.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "savitri",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "And I remember the moment, in that tent, when I looked in her eyes and saw that she would never laugh again.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I did that. For this.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "For this.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "Pillai. You do not usually visit this part of the fort.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I do not usually find two Europeans praying to their god in a kingdom that just surrendered itself to ours.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DUARTE"
   ],
   "text": "The Maharaja permits us this small space. We ask nothing of him but the right to serve.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "And to pray. A man needs something beyond walls and accounts.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "Otherwise the walls become a prison and the accounts become chains.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "A Maratha cavalryman, a Dutch artillerist, a Portuguese priest.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Twenty years ago our peoples were killing each other across three continents. Now we stand under the same banner.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-02",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "The banner does not ask where we came from. Only where we stand now.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DUARTE"
   ],
   "text": "I do not do this to convert you. It is the only blessing I know how to give.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "DUARTE"
   ],
   "text": "And you have earned a blessing, Ananthan Pillai. Whatever you believe.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "Even Ramayyan visited once. He spent the whole time examining the stonework rather than the altar.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "DUARTE"
   ],
   "text": "He said the mortar was acceptable. High praise, from him.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "When I die, I have asked to be buried here. In this fort I helped design. Under a stone that says I served Travancore.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "We are all servants now. You serve Padmanabha through the king. I serve Padmanabha through the walls.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "DE LANNOY"
   ],
   "text": "It is a strange household. But it holds.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "duarte",
    "eustachius",
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "OFFICER"
   ],
   "text": "What was Travancore like, before it was Travancore?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "It was smaller. And more divided. And more free, in some ways.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And more vulnerable.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-03",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "OFFICER"
   ],
   "text": "Do you miss it?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
